/* Chained by the manifest's sequence: after 3-8. */

## The shore

@narrator: Past the Hollow Keep the ground stops. What comes after it is water, and every wave carries a lantern.
@lumi{emotion="surprised"}: Those are the lanterns from the throne room. They floated all the way out here.
@lumi{when="holds('learned', ['lanternSea'])"}: You read the codex page, didn't you? Then you know: every lantern is a wish somebody gave up on.
@lumi{when="!holds('learned', ['lanternSea'])"}: I don't know what they are. There's a page about it in the Archive, if you're the reading type.
::assert{learned(lanternSea)}
<branch id="c4s1Boat" prompt="A boat is tied to the last post.">
  <choice id="row" label="Row out.">
    @lumi: I'll steer. You row. That's how partnerships work.
  </choice>
  <choice id="wait" label="Wait for the tide.">
    @lumi: Fine by me. The tide's never late. That's the one thing it's good at.
  </choice>
</branch>
